    "body": "Fixes #8126.\n\nThis is close to untestable, since we already have a cpp_stl_string_cpp11 test and that doesn't trigger the issue. I think most standard library implementations don't guard the string_view header so it just works even on lower versions. We'd therefore need an old compiler that doesn't have it at all.\n\nI don't believe there are any other cases where we cimport something that requires a different C++ version in our libcpp wrappings.",
    "closed_at": null,
